in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/colorado/san-miguel-county"],["ARC or PLC in San Miguel County","/arc-plc/colorado/san-miguel-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, May to June has come in under 90% of normal in 38 of the 75 years since 1951 on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 13 grids. It is also the driest pair, with a normal of 1.98 inches. In 2026 so far, the county&rsquo;s middle value got 45% of normal in May to June and 49% in February to March. Grid 21384 had its driest year in 1989 at 48%.</p>"}
